[136.048823, "o", "voke its sessions, and review what it did after Nov\r\n\u001b[6C22 03:12.\r\n   2. \u001b[1mBlock:\u001b[m add \u001b[37m 198.51.100.22 \u001b[m to the perimeter blocklist.\r\n   3. \u001b[1mCheck the other accounts:\u001b[m about 300 accounts were sprayed. Reset or watch any with a success from this\r\n\u001b[6CIP.\r\n   4. \u001b[1mDetection:\u001b[m the notebook's \u001b[37m detection \u001b[m cell produced a daily saved-search SPL. Over 90 days the rule\r\n      flagged only this IP.                                  \u001b[48C┃\r\r\n\r\n   I can create that as \u001b[37m demo_password_spray_daily \u001b[m in the \u001b[37m search \u001b[m app with \u001b[37m splunkctl \u001b[m. As you require,\r\n   I'll run it without \u001b[37m --yes \u001b[m first and show you the command for approval.\r\u001b[6B \u001b[1m←\u001b[m open sidebar · Interactive · Manual Approval · \u001b[1m/\u001b[m commands · \u001b[1m?\u001b[m help · \u001b[1mtab\u001b[m next tab\u001b[30;3H\u001b[?25h"]
